{
  "name": "WF-1 · Lead Intake + AI Qualification + HubSpot Sync",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 · LEAD COMES IN\n\nYour website form sends the lead here.\n\n**Setup:** copy the Production URL from this node and paste it into your form's \"Webhook / POST URL\" field.\n\nSend the fields as a **flat body** (not nested). The next node accepts both shapes anyway, so a nested payload will not break it.",
        "height": 240,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "8627dac7-f1dd-4e76-b6b3-18c34fb7a447",
      "name": "Sticky · Intake",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1040,
        48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 · ⚙️ EDIT THIS ONE NODE\n\nAll the settings a client ever needs to change live in the **⚙️ SETTINGS** node.\n\nNothing else in this workflow has a hardcoded email, channel or ID.\n\nChange the values there, save, done.",
        "height": 208,
        "width": 300,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "f9f2e42d-ac6d-4289-8a55-8046cc3b6dc9",
      "name": "Sticky · Settings",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -688,
        48
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 · SAFETY GATE\n\n**Normalize** flattens whatever the form sent into clean fields, and never returns `undefined` — every field falls back to an empty string.\n\n**Required Data Valid?** checks the email exists and is a real email shape.\n\nBad payload → an honest 400 reply, and the workflow stops. It never reaches the AI or your CRM.",
        "height": 224,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "745dfbf4-18fd-4a66-9e8e-e62a84d95faf",
      "name": "Sticky · Validation",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -320,
        -32
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4 · DEDUPLICATION\n\nLooks the email up in HubSpot **before** doing anything.\n\nIf the search fails or finds nothing, the node is set to **continue** rather than stop — so a CRM hiccup can never lose you a lead.\n\nReturning leads are flagged `is_returning = true` so the AI knows this is a second touch, and Slack says so in the alert.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "8f7c249e-b22a-4f31-bd2c-9713292bb201",
      "name": "Sticky · Dedup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        96,
        -64
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 5 · AI QUALIFICATION\n\nThe AI returns **strict JSON only** — score, tier, reason, intent, and a ready-to-send reply.\n\nThe **Qualification Schema** node forces that shape, so no Code node is needed to parse the answer and the output can never arrive as loose text.\n\nIf the AI is down, this node continues with an error output instead of killing the run — the lead still reaches HubSpot.",
        "height": 260,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "cf0d28cb-ecfc-4034-82e6-81d473d92352",
      "name": "Sticky · AI",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        528,
        32
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 6 · CRM SYNC\n\nOne node, one job: create the contact, or update it if the email already exists.\n\nScore, tier, reason and source are written to HubSpot so your sales team sees the AI's verdict inside the contact record.\n\n**Before first run:** create these 4 custom contact properties in HubSpot (internal names exactly as written in the sticky note below this one).",
        "height": 244,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "25839b4d-de37-4f0b-bd85-339349656805",
      "name": "Sticky · CRM",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1024,
        128
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### HubSpot custom properties to create once\n\nSettings → Properties → Create property (object: Contact)\n\n| Label | Internal name | Type |\n|---|---|---|\n| AI Lead Score | `ai_lead_score` | Number |\n| AI Lead Tier | `ai_lead_tier` | Single-line text |\n| AI Qualification Reason | `ai_qualification_reason` | Multi-line text |\n| Lead Source Detail | `lead_source_detail` | Single-line text |\n\nIf you skip this, the upsert still works — the four values are simply not stored.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "ca22d393-ec1a-490d-8c89-c7cd9daecba6",
      "name": "Sticky · HubSpot Properties",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1184,
        672
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 7 · ROUTING\n\n**HOT** → Slack alert + AI reply containing your booking link\n**WARM** → AI reply only, sales is not interrupted\n**COLD** → logged to the nurture sheet, nobody is emailed\n\nThresholds live in ⚙️ SETTINGS, not here.\n\n**Hard rule:** a lead can never reach HOT with no budget stated, even if the AI's raw score clears the threshold — it is capped at WARM instead, and the reason field says why. This keeps sales alerts trustworthy and keeps tier stable even if the AI's wording varies between runs.\n\nThe **UNTIERED** output catches any lead the AI failed to grade at all.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "7b3f3837-23ca-4a94-ac13-552d4538b720",
      "name": "Sticky · Routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1376,
        -48
      ]
    },
