    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## WHY THIS WORKFLOW DOES NOT THROW \"Can't determine which item\"\n\nEvery cross-node reference uses `$('Node Name').first().json.field` — never `.item.json`.\n\n`.item` asks n8n to trace which input item produced the current one. After an AI node that trace can break, and you get the paired-item error that is impossible to debug from the UI.\n\nOne webhook call = one lead = one item, so `.first()` is always the same item — and it can never fail.\n\n**If you add nodes: keep using `.first()`.**\n\n---\n\n**Second rule: never `.first()` a node that has more than one output (IF / Switch).**\n\n`$('SomeIfNode').first()` silently reads output 0 only. If the run took the other branch, that output has zero items and the field becomes `null` with no error shown.\n\nFix: reference the single-output node that runs **before** the branch instead — e.g. `$('HubSpot · Find Existing Contact')`, not `$('Returning Lead?')`.",
